.TH tar_set_gnu_extension_limits 3 "November 2025" "libtar" "C Library Calls"
.SH NAME
tar_set_gnu_extension_limits \- set per-record GNU extension resource limits
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <libtar.h>
.P
.BI "int tar_set_gnu_extension_limits(TAR *" t ", size_t " bytes ", size_t " headers ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR tar_set_gnu_extension_limits ()
sets the per-logical-record budget for GNU longname (\fBL\fR) and
longlink (\fBK\fR) extension headers read by
.BR th_read ().
.I bytes
is the maximum total declared payload length; every declaration counts,
including copies later overridden.
.I headers
is the maximum number of \fBL\fR/\fBK\fR extension headers; repeated
headers count as well.

Handles created by
.BR tar_open ()
and
.BR tar_fdopen ()
default to 1 MiB and 64 headers.  Both arguments must be positive.
The call is intended between two
.BR th_read ()
calls.  It does not reset accumulation state and does not clear a sticky
read-error state.
.SH "RETURN VALUE"
Returns 0 on success.  Otherwise returns \-1 with
.I errno
set to
.BR EINVAL
and leaves the handle and previous settings unchanged.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EINVAL
.I t
is NULL, or
.I bytes
or
.I headers
is zero.
.PP
An exceeded budget is reported by the following
.BR th_read ()
as \-1 with
.IR errno = E2BIG .
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR th_read (3),
.BR tar_open (3)
